		<P CLASS="Text_ind" STYLE="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:24pt;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">Any dispute arising from or in connection with this Agreement shall first be resolved through good<FONT CLASS="nobreak">-faith</FONT> consultation. If the Parties fail to resolve the dispute within thirty (30)&#x00a0;days after any Party requests consultation, either Party may submit the dispute to the China International Economic and Trade Arbitration Commission for arbitration in accordance with its then effective arbitration rules. The place of arbitration shall be Changzhou. The arbitration language shall be Chinese. The arbitral award shall be final and binding on both Parties.</P>
